  "meta": {
    "tier": {
      "deletion": "soft",
      "note": "Rank order and base_rate (integer UGX per confirmed session); criteria is JSON text read by the monthly tier job. Soft-deleted tiers keep their unique name until restored or retention. Soft delete (M02 rule): active_key = lower-case name while the tier is live, set to null on soft delete (soft_delete_patch), so a deleted tier name can be re-created."
    },
    "tier_history": {
      "deletion": "immutable",
      "note": "One row per tier change (TIR-4), approved by an admin; corrections are new rows. First assignment has no from_tier_id."
    },
    "bonus_rule": {
      "deletion": "soft",
      "note": "Configurable bonus per confirmed session (TIR-5); amount is integer UGX; conditions is JSON text."
    },
    "invoice": {
      "deletion": "hard",
      "note": "Created at period start. Unique (subscription, period start) makes the period job idempotent. parent_id is the payer (read grant). Voiding is a status, not a delete. Never soft-deleted (a soft delete would either hide a financial/idempotency record or free its unique value): the lifecycle is the status column; only the retention job hard-deletes it, after the retention period (DP-6, SR 5.5). Voiding is the status void. Retention: payment records are kept for the tax-law period (DP-6) even against a DP-5 deletion request; the conflict is Q4/Q16-17 in docs/legal/lawyer-brief.md (C04)."
    },
    "payment": {
      "deletion": "hard",
      "note": "idempotency_key UNIQUE (NFR-8): the core service claims the key by create (409 = already requested). provider_reference is unique per provider once known (NULLs allowed until then). raw_callback stores the verified provider callback verbatim (PAY-1..3, SR 7.8). Provider is free text on purpose: the owner has not chosen providers. Never soft-deleted (a soft delete would either hide a financial/idempotency record or free its unique value): the lifecycle is the status column; only the retention job hard-deletes it, after the retention period (DP-6, SR 5.5). idempotency_key and provider_reference stay claimed forever (NFR-8). Retention: payment records are kept for the tax-law period (DP-6) even against a DP-5 deletion request; the conflict is Q4/Q16-17 in docs/legal/lawyer-brief.md (C04)."
    },
    "earning": {
      "deletion": "hard",
      "note": "Created when a session is confirmed (SR 5.4). dedupe_key (e.g. <session>:<type>[:<rule>]) is unique so confirmation retries cannot double-pay. adjustment amounts may be negative. batch_id is set when the weekly payout batch takes the earning. Never soft-deleted (a soft delete would either hide a financial/idempotency record or free its unique value): the lifecycle is the status column; only the retention job hard-deletes it, after the retention period (DP-6, SR 5.5). dedupe_key stays claimed (no double pay); cancel = status void."
    },
    "payout_batch": {
      "deletion": "soft",
      "note": "Weekly batch (SR 7.9). active_key = period start date while the batch is not cancelled, NULL after, unique: one live batch per period (M01 active_key pattern). SEC-11: approved_by plus a distinct second confirmation (confirmed_by/confirmed_at); the core service rejects approver == confirmer."
    },
    "payout": {
      "deletion": "hard",
      "note": "One payout per (batch, teacher); idempotency_key UNIQUE (NFR-8). Failures retry on the same row and end in needs_ops. The teacher's payout number lives with the teacher profile (re-verification and 48 h hold, SEC-11, are a core-service rule outside this ticket). Never soft-deleted (a soft delete would either hide a financial/idempotency record or free its unique value): the lifecycle is the status column; only the retention job hard-deletes it, after the retention period (DP-6, SR 5.5). idempotency_key stays claimed (NFR-8); failure = status. Retention: payment records are kept for the tax-law period (DP-6) even against a DP-5 deletion request; the conflict is Q4/Q16-17 in docs/legal/lawyer-brief.md (C04)."
    },
    "ledger_account": {
      "deletion": "hard",
      "note": "SR 7.10 minimum accounts plus one teacher payable per teacher (teacher_id set). code is unique, e.g. cash:mtn_momo, teacher_payable:<teacher_id>. Balances are derived from ledger_entry, never stored. Never soft-deleted (a soft delete would either hide a financial/idempotency record or free its unique value): the lifecycle is the status column; only the retention job hard-deletes it, after the retention period (DP-6, SR 5.5). code is never reused; retire with active=false. The M04 migration seeds no rows: the ledger service ($01 #76) must create the SR 7.10 accounts (parent receivables, cash at MTN MoMo / Airtel / card gateway, teacher payables per teacher via teacher_id, platform revenue, refunds and credits, provider fees)."
    },
    "ledger_transaction": {
      "deletion": "immutable",
      "append_only": true,
      "note": "APPEND-ONLY header of a balanced posting (SR 7.10). Core-service rules (owner: $01 #76, not enforceable in Appwrite): sum(debit amounts) == sum(credit amounts) == total_amount, entry_count == number of lines, all in one currency, integer UGX > 0; idempotency_key unique so a retried posting cannot double post; corrections are a new transaction with kind=reversal and reverses_transaction_id (unique: reversed once). reference_type/reference_id are polymorphic (payment, earning, payout...). INTENDED insert-only via AppendOnlyRepository (opt-in, not wired yet: nothing uses it; see appwrite/README.md).",
      "non_fk": {
        "reference_id": "polymorphic reference to payment/earning/payout/invoice rows, discriminated by reference_type"
      }
    },
    "ledger_entry": {
      "deletion": "immutable",
      "append_only": true,
      "note": "APPEND-ONLY line of a transaction: one side (debit or credit) and a positive integer UGX amount. Unique (transaction_id, line). No client write permission. INTENDED insert-only via AppendOnlyRepository (opt-in, not wired yet: nothing uses it; see appwrite/README.md). Write all lines first, the header last so a crash leaves no header over partial lines (reconciliation job flags orphan lines).",
      "non_fk": {
        "reference_id": "polymorphic reference, discriminated by reference_type"
      }
    },
    "feedback": {
      "deletion": "soft",
      "note": "Parent/child feedback after a session (SR 5.4, SAF-3). child_rating 1..5 (face rating). teacher_id/child_id denormalised from the session so tier evaluation can query without a join. A 'something felt wrong' answer additionally creates a safeguarding_case in the core service. Soft delete (M02 rule): active_key = '<session_id>:<parent_id>' while live, null after soft delete: one live feedback per session and parent."
    }
  },
